Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.79,0:00:07.75,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.75,0:00:09.78,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Chimera Shadow Garden.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.09,0:00:18.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Esoteric Technique: Hollow Wicker Basket!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.20,0:00:26.84,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Hollow Wicker Basket is the origin of\NNew Shadow Style's "Simple Domain."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.84,0:00:28.97,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It possesses the ability\Nto neutralize a domain
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.97,0:00:32.49,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and counter its guaranteed-hit factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.49,0:00:34.48,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Too bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.18,0:00:38.79,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,The "Domain Amplification" used\Nby Jogo and Hanami in Shibuya
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.79,0:00:40.72,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,utilized a domain capable of harboring
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.72,0:00:43.26,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,a guaranteed-hit, \Nguaranteed-kill technique...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.85,0:00:47.86,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why is it hitting me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.86,0:00:51.16,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,...and intentionally left out\Ntheir cursed techniques
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.16,0:00:55.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,to leave space for Gojo's\Ncursed technique to flow into,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.07,0:00:57.16,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,neutralizing his Limitless.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.44,0:01:00.08,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, Hollow Wicker\NBasket and Simple Domain
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.08,0:01:03.50,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,aren't capable of neutralizing\Nthe cursed technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.84,0:01:07.89,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,They work by neutralizing a barrier\Nimbued with a cursed technique
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.89,0:01:12.34,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,to nullify the imbued technique's\Nguaranteed-hit effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.88,0:01:18.40,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, Fushiguro's\Ndomain is incomplete.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.40,0:01:20.50,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You're not sneering anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.50,0:01:22.27,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Damn brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.96,0:01:29.41,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,By transposing his domain onto\Nthe space of the gymnasium,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.41,0:01:31.75,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,he managed to force it to close,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.75,0:01:34.61,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,but it's not imbued with a\Nguaranteed-hit technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.24,0:01:38.19,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Don't act like you've won!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.48,0:01:41.09,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.09,0:01:42.95,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Chimera Shadow Garden
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.95,0:01:47.17,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,currently just extends his\NTen Shadows Technique,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.17,0:01:52.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and draws out 120% of\Nhis latent potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.58,0:01:54.96,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, that very imperfection
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.96,0:01:57.55,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,is what caught Reggie Star off-guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.55,0:02:02.13,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Both his clones and his shikigami had\Nphysical forms before striking me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.13,0:02:03.66,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means this barrier
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.66,0:02:06.14,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}isn't imbued with a\Nguaranteed-hit technique!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.52,0:02:10.62,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}The domain's buff to his technique's\Nabilities is no joke, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.62,0:02:14.00,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is even worse to deal with than\Na simple guaranteed-hit domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.00,0:02:17.83,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}If he pulls out that elephant\Nhere and drenches me in water,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.83,0:02:20.96,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}it'll halve my options,\Nand I'll probably lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.58,0:02:29.95,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}But...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.95,0:02:32.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}it's so like me
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.15,0:02:35.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}to make sure that won't happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.97,0:02:37.01,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Nue!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.81,0:02:43.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Too slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.06,0:02:48.78,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.98,0:02:53.30,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,For a while now,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.30,0:02:57.32,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I've had to reinforce my footing with\Ncursed energy to avoid getting sucked in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.75,0:03:05.28,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The whole bottom of this domain\Nis your shadow, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.29,0:03:10.44,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Being able to store and remove yourself\Nand objects is convenient, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.44,0:03:13.18,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But one thing nagged at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.18,0:03:15.69,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,"He doesn't have many weapons."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.69,0:03:19.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I've only seen you use\None paltry cursed tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.01,0:03:20.65,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Either it has a low capacity
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.65,0:03:25.23,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,and you need to reserve space\Nfor yourself at all times,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.23,0:03:31.73,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,or you're forced to bear the weight of\Nthings stored in your shadow yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.50,0:03:35.48,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Looks like the latter was spot-on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.90,0:03:39.49,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Now I've turned the design\Nof your domain against you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.49,0:03:44.41,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,With three passenger cars,\Nyour current weight is 2.4 tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.81,0:03:47.21,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Looks like your clones weren't\Nable to tolerate it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.21,0:03:50.42,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,but can you still produce your shikigami?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.16,0:03:54.45,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Either way, I'll just\Nneed to mind my footing
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.45,0:03:58.96,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,as I keep adding weight until\Nyou're crushed under it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.47,0:04:03.75,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Are you stupid?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.75,0:04:05.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.15,0:04:08.70,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Even if it's incomplete,\Na domain is still a domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.35,0:04:12.94,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,My shadow's above us, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.74,0:04:27.19,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Which of us will get crushed first,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.76,0:04:29.26,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Reggie?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.83,0:06:09.17,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's said that a typical human will\Nlose consciousness at five to six Gs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.83,0:06:11.57,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,2.4 tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.17,0:06:15.32,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,As Fushiguro weighed 60 kilograms,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:19.47,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,that meant he was currently\Nsuffering 40 Gs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.26,0:06:24.08,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,In order to prevent his blood from\Npooling in his legs from the high Gs
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.08,0:06:27.20,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and depriving his brain of blood flow,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.20,0:06:29.64,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Fushiguro was lowering his posture
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.64,0:06:31.92,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and reinforcing his body\Nwith cursed energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.92,0:06:34.78,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,paying special attention to his legs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.06,0:06:40.53,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,A mature African elephant\Nweighs three to six tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.93,0:06:45.21,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,With the domain's improvement\Nto his technique's accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.21,0:06:48.59,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Max Elephant accurately\Nrecreated its real weight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.92,0:06:54.82,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Under that weight, Reggie Star's right\Nfibula and heel bone were cracked.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.03,0:06:58.76,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Both of them faced
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.76,0:07:02.62,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,the possibility of being crushed\Nto death at any second.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.07,0:07:06.00,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I screwed up!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.00,0:07:08.84,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could have won if I'd kept\Nthe trucks in reserve!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.84,0:07:10.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.33,0:07:13.06,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I got splashed with some\Nwater at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.06,0:07:15.00,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}but my trump card's still safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.00,0:07:19.04,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could slip into his shadow and\Nrecreate my trump card inside it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.04,0:07:21.44,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}That would crush him!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.39,0:07:24.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.43,0:07:26.82,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}If he's not dismissing his domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.82,0:07:32.38,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}that means anything in his shadow is\Nstuck there after he dismisses his domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.83,0:07:36.93,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What if I'm stuck in his shadow\Nforever after he dies?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.56,0:07:40.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's it like inside his shadow, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.07,0:07:43.04,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}It looks like a liquid,\Nbut can I breathe in it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.04,0:07:44.06,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can I float?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.51,0:07:48.56,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No. Submerging into his\Nshadow is too risky.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.56,0:07:51.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}So while stuck in this state...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.16,0:07:55.55,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to pull out my trump\Ncard and activate it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.52,0:08:02.62,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Contractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.40,0:08:24.11,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I didn't make it in time!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.11,0:08:27.26,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}And there's no air inside his shadow!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.71,0:08:31.54,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No buoyancy or resistance, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.24,0:08:38.90,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm just... sinking!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.04,0:08:43.79,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}My consciousness... is fading...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.49,0:08:51.85,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not yet! Endure it a little longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.85,0:08:54.72,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait until I'm sure he's dead\Nbefore dismissing the domain!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.72,0:08:57.60,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I can expel what's in my shadow!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.18,0:09:32.71,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The things I recreate
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.71,0:09:36.92,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,disappear soon after carrying\Nout the command I give them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.92,0:09:40.18,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I hadn't given the cars\NI sank a command, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.18,0:09:43.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I didn't want them\Ndisappearing, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.43,0:09:46.51,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That meant I could still\Nissue them a command.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.51,0:09:49.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,"Take me and rise up!"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.33,0:09:53.90,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The weight of one car is gone\Nnow, but that saved my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.80,0:09:59.50,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'll admit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.50,0:10:01.44,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You're strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.95,0:10:07.27,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But I'm stronger!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.27,0:10:10.79,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Contractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.87,0:10:21.34,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,A 132-square-foot, \Ntwo-story wooden frame structure!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.34,0:10:24.77,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The framework alone weighs\Nat least thirty tons!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.77,0:10:27.61,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Get crushed!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.47,0:11:02.24,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What happened?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.24,0:11:04.81,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did I fall into his shadow again?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.09,0:11:07.50,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.50,0:11:09.16,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm in actual water!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.16,0:11:10.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}How?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.18,0:11:12.32,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's heavy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.32,0:11:15.11,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that brat trying to strangle me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.44,0:11:17.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}What power!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.31,0:11:19.05,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, that's wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.05,0:11:22.42,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's from the weight of\Nthe two cars I added!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.60,0:11:25.73,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.28,0:11:28.06,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This time, I'm sinking!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.69,0:11:31.96,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to dismiss\NContractual Re-Creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.14,0:11:51.76,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.76,0:11:53.76,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is a community gymnasium!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.76,0:11:56.97,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the gymnasium's basement\Nis a heated swimming pool!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.79,0:12:02.57,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did he flee into his shadow\Nand dismiss his domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.57,0:12:06.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}forcing me to destroy the floor\Nand plunge into the pool?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.75,0:12:13.08,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You can't use your receipts when\Nthey're that soaked, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.19,0:12:20.59,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He waited instead of \Npursuing me immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.59,0:12:24.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He let his technique recover after\Nexhausting it with his domain, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.87,0:12:27.98,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Are you sure about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.74,0:12:32.47,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'm betting you can't produce \Nshikigami anymore either, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.65,0:12:35.16,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.16,0:12:38.14,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You do understand what \Ncomes next, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.65,0:12:43.26,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}He'll use a shikigami other than that dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.26,0:12:45.54,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}But none of them can\Ndeal a decisive blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.54,0:12:47.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}So use it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.35,0:12:51.16,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\i1}The moment you let up,\NI'll finish you with a counter!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.60,0:13:46.37,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Demon Dogs isn't weak enough\Nto let that stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.38,0:13:52.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Sorcerers are all liars, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.14,0:14:09.97,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.97,0:14:11.18,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,the pool...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.83,0:14:16.38,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,All to convince me you couldn't\Nuse that dog anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.38,0:14:20.16,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You didn't flee into this gymnasium.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.16,0:14:21.80,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You lured me into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.40,0:14:24.45,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,To think I'd let a modern sorcerer,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.45,0:14:28.34,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,and a brat at that, get the better of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.00,0:14:33.83,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Even if I wanted to flee, Nue can't\Nfly with someone for very long.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.83,0:14:36.10,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I've struggled with that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.82,0:14:45.71,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What's your relation to {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.61,0:14:51.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Tengen?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.45,0:14:55.08,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.08,0:14:57.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,They would still be alive, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.07,0:15:00.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That shut-in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.35,0:15:02.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Yeah? That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.24,0:15:08.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Reggie said {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}'s claims about\Nthe Culling Game's goals were a bluff.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.24,0:15:12.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should probably consider\Nthe possibility that
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.34,0:15:16.33,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}{*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} and Kenjaku are secretly\Nconnected and lied about their goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.00,0:15:19.24,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}but that doesn't seem\Nlikely from his reaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.41,0:15:28.88,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Kogane, give him all my points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.36,0:15:30.58,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.03,0:15:36.34,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have received \N41 points from Reggie Star.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.34,0:15:37.82,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What are you plotting?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.55,0:15:41.46,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That's an awful thing to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.46,0:15:44.27,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It's my good deed before I die.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.97,0:15:47.70,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I'm just a spectator.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.70,0:15:50.35,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I was never close friends with Kenjaku.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.88,0:15:54.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I think doing this will\Nmake things interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.94,0:15:56.82,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That's my intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.28,0:16:00.19,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.19,0:16:02.66,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You did kill me, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.31,0:16:10.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Let fate toy with you\Na bit, and die a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.16,0:16:35.79,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have gained five points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.86,0:16:50.18,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Did I get him?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.71,0:16:52.89,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,No! Don't let your guard down!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.43,0:16:55.82,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,He's tough!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.82,0:16:57.41,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,What the hell?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.84,0:16:59.99,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Why are you covered in lotion?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.99,0:17:01.45,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,It could be sauce.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.45,0:17:02.92,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Shut up! Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.47,0:17:07.12,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Wait, it really is sauce?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.39,0:17:08.19,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.19,0:17:10.11,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Seriously, what's with this guy?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.11,0:17:12.24,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've blown him up several times!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.24,0:17:14.44,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I feel like I've killed him five times!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.83,0:17:17.41,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}So how does he have so little damage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.60,0:17:20.01,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,You hate sauce?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.52,0:17:23.24,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}His first injury healed \Nat some point, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.74,0:17:27.72,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}But he hasn't shown any signs of using \Nreverse cursed techniques like I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.35,0:17:30.47,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.03,0:17:32.52,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Hazenoki{*}{*-sama}.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.52,0:17:33.83,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.83,0:17:36.99,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Reggie Star{*}{*-sama} has just died.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.67,0:17:42.22,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Oh? What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.22,0:17:43.55,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,I'm going home.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.55,0:17:44.92,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,I'm sick of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.92,0:17:46.01,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.01,0:17:47.14,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Take a bath!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.14,0:17:48.46,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,And brush your teeth!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.35,0:17:54.00,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Hey, man! Give me your points!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.44,0:17:55.67,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Stop following me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.67,0:17:59.36,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,Please! Just think of it\Nas going with the flow!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.36,0:18:00.35,Default,Hazenoki,0,0,0,,Die.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.66,0:18:03.38,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Takaba's cursed technique, Comedian,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.38,0:18:07.76,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,makes whatever he's convinced\Nwould be funny a reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.76,0:18:11.86,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's a technique capable of\Nopposing even Gojo Satoru.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.44,0:18:18.37,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Yet Takaba doesn't know anything\Nabout his own technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.79,0:18:28.82,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't get it! I don't get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.82,0:18:32.25,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ever since I became an adult,\NI hardly understand anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.92,0:18:40.75,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've heard that all men are wolves,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.75,0:18:44.93,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}but it's always those wolves who take\Ncare of the confusing stuff for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.17,0:18:51.81,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}If those wolves will handle everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.81,0:18:54.67,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}then I don't need to\Nthink about anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.67,0:18:57.36,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I'm so cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.58,0:19:07.65,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Those wolves always... always...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.29,0:19:18.73,Default,Tsumiki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't, Megumi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.96,0:19:27.15,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,You'll spare me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.52,0:19:37.14,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Shut up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.46,0:19:42.45,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Damn sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.99,0:20:05.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Events progressed quickly\Nin the Sendai Colony,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.07,0:20:08.71,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,far outstripping those\Nof the Tokyo Colony
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.71,0:20:10.42,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and becoming especially fierce.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.66,0:20:17.27,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Dhruv Lakdawalla. Current points: 91.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.27,0:20:19.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,This is his second incarnation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.80,0:20:22.51,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He's an old man who\Nsingle-handedly conquered
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.51,0:20:25.27,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,this archipelago during\Nthe Civil War of Wa.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.87,0:20:28.34,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He possesses two autonomous shikigami,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.34,0:20:32.57,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and the orbit of those shikigami\Ndetermines his domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.51,0:20:40.03,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Ishigori Ryu. Current points: 77.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.71,0:20:45.13,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He's the cannon with the greatest\Ncursed energy output among the Players.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.76,0:20:50.43,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Uro Takako. Current points: 70.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.13,0:20:54.12,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,She was originally the captain of\Nthe Sun, Moon, and Stars Squad,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.12,0:20:56.73,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,a squad of assassins serving\Ndirectly under the Fujiwara Clan.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.26,0:21:00.52,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,She possesses a technique that \Nallows her to manipulate "the sky."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.74,0:21:06.02,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Kurourushi. Current points: 54.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.02,0:21:08.86,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's a cockroach cursed\Nspirit that Kenjaku freed
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.86,0:21:12.02,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,from the control of cursed\Nspirit manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.02,0:21:15.88,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It ranks as a special-grade\N(already registered).
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.00,0:21:20.84,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,It's currently lying dormant until\Ncertain conditions are met.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.16,0:21:23.79,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,There was no alliance between them,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.79,0:21:27.59,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,but their complex compatibility\Nand opposing strength
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.59,0:21:30.05,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,led them into a three—no,\Na four-way stalemate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.58,0:21:33.34,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,But one of those pillars
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.79,0:21:36.16,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,has fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.60,0:21:42.39,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Okkotsu Yuta. Current points: 35.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.04,0:21:45.48,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Three months after the \NNight Parade of a Hundred Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.48,0:21:47.98,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,he had blossomed as a\Nspecial-grade sorcerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.98,0:21:51.53,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He was a modern sorcerer\Nrivaling Gojo Satoru
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.53,0:21:53.07,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,in unusual abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.55,0:23:28.40,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,I'll obtain 400 points on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.40,0:23:31.08,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Yuta, which would you like?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.08,0:23:32.31,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,It's called Kurourushi!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.31,0:23:32.81,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,Give me everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.81,0:23:35.34,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Give me back Yuta!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.34,0:23:38.43,Default,Okkotsu,0,0,0,,{*}Teach{*Sensei}, I won't let you kill\Nyour best friend twice.
